course: dictionary
lesson: 10796
title: Vanishing: gone from sight, or almost gone
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «The Cheshire Cat keeps vanishing, beginning with its tail and ending with its grin.» The word vanishing tells you the cat keeps disappearing from sight, and the clue that it starts with the tail shows it can go slowly, one part at a time.
explain: Vanishing can also mean becoming fewer and smaller until almost gone. Look for clues like «habitats» and «in danger» in a science text: if a home for animals is in danger, it may be vanishing.
explain: In art, the words «parallel lines seem to meet at a vanishing point» are about drawing. Ask what would fit: a vanishing point is a place, not a trick, so the meaning is the spot where lines seem to meet.
fact: Vanish is the basic verb; vanishing is one of its forms.
fact: «Vanishing» can mean disappearing suddenly or completely, so you cannot see it any more.
fact: «Vanishing» can also mean becoming fewer or smaller until almost gone, as in «vanishing forests».
fact: In art and maths, the vanishing point is where parallel lines seem to meet in a perspective drawing.
fact: A good check is to swap in the word disappearing: if the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning.
exercise: The Cheshire Cat keeps vanishing. What does vanishing mean here? | Growing bigger and brighter | *Disappearing so you cannot see it | Falling asleep under a tree | Singing loudly to the children
exercise: «Vanishing forests» are forests that are becoming what? | Covered in deep snow | *Fewer and smaller, until almost gone | Painted in bright colours | Taller every year
exercise: Find and copy the word that means «seem to meet» in «parallel lines seem to meet at a vanishing point». | parallel | *meet | lines | point
test: A magician's vanishing trick made the coin disappear in a flash. What does vanishing show? | Something grew very large | Something was painted | *Something disappeared from sight | Something was seen clearly
test: Which word could replace vanishing in «vanishing species» without changing the meaning much? | *Disappearing | Shining | Growing | Ringing
exam: In a drawing, where is the vanishing point? | Beside the artist's signature | *Where parallel lines seem to meet | At the top of the page only | Where the paint runs out
